~ initialize_local_variables

=> start

~ start
#you can barely see part of Micah through the window for a second, and then you can hear the door open but you can't see anyone; after a few seconds, you can see his head pop up from under the table; he sneaked up on you.
#sound effect needed
...[do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_open", -20)][wait=3]
Micah: [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_jumpscare", -12.0)]Raagh!
- You scared the shit out of me. 
	Micah: [#sprite=happy]Hahaha! Got you. 
	- Don't ever do that again.
		Micah: [#sprite=happy]Can't promise anything. Sneaking up on people is kind of my thing. => whothehell
	- Sure did. Prepare for retaliation!
		Micah: Not sure that's even a word. Sarah's been teaching me, and now I've got a big vo-ca-bu-lary now. 
		Micah: [#sprite=upset]But I've never heard of this one. So you might wanna double check that. 
		Micah: [#sprite=happy]Either way, I'm always prepared for everything! => whothehell
- Who the hell are you?
	Micah: [#sprite=upset]Who the hell are YOU?
	- I'm the Shopkeeper's new apprentice. 
		Micah: Oh, finally. Perhaps the old man won't be complaining all day anymore. 
		Micah: [#sprite=happy]I'm the delivery boy. Future shopkeeper myself. I'll steal your job from you when I grow up. 
		- You Gifted yourself?
			Micah: Not yet. But I'm The Goddess's most devoted follower. There's no way She won't give it to me too, someday.
			Micah: Anyway, for now, I'm the one bringing you items every morning. You cleanse them, I take them back the next day. => stupid
		- I'd like to see you try.
			Micah: [#sprite=happy]Oh, don't worry. You will. 
			Micah: Anyway, for now, I'm the one bringing you items every morning. You cleanse them, I take them back the next day. => stupid
	- I'm the Goddess's chosen one. I'm here at Her command, serving as an apprentice to the Shopkeeper. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") == 6]
		Micah: [#sprite=upset]Uh huh. If you say so. 
		Micah: I'm the delivery boy. I bring items here every morning. You cleanse them, I take them back the next day. => stupid
	- Just someone running from the Cullings, same as everyone else. I work here now. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 5]
		Micah: Yeah, we get more and more people coming here for that same reason.
		Micah: [#sprite=upset]Wonder how many of y'all are true believers, though. 
		Micah: I'm the delivery boy. I bring items here every morning. You cleanse them, I take them back the next day. => stupid
	- I asked first.
		Micah: [#sprite=upset]Fine. Pretty sure I know who you are, anyway. 
		Micah: [#sprite=happy]I'm the delivery boy. Future shopkeeper, once the old man kicks the bucket. 
		- That's not nice.
			Micah: Oh, the old man doesn't mind. He's not a sourpuss. That's how we usually talk. 
			Micah: Anyway, for now, I'm the one bringing you items every morning. You cleanse them, I take them back the next day. => stupid
		- Ambitious, aren't you? You Gifted too?
			Micah: Not yet. But I'm the Goddess's most devoted follower. There's no way She won't give it to me too.
			Micah: Anyway, for now, I'm the one bringing you items every morning. You cleanse them, I take them back the next day. => stupid
